**Finding: compliant (at fallback).**

Section 8.1 carries a full Vendor-side IP indemnity in our favour, with:
- express defend/indemnify/hold harmless duty running to Corio **and its Customers**;
- third-party claims that the Software infringes patent, copyright, trademark or trade secret;
- standard procedure (prompt written notice, tender of control, cooperation, with our right to join with own counsel);
- complete remedy ladder — procure, replace/modify, else terminate and refund a pro-rated portion of fees paid;
- exclusions (Section 8.2) narrower than the fallback permits — only non-Documentation use and third-party modification, with no combination or specification carve-outs.

The 3× super-cap element is unnecessary here: Section 9 twice carves "LIABILITY ARISING UNDER SECTION 8" out of both the 12-month fees cap and the consequential-damages waiver, so the indemnity is effectively uncapped — a better outcome than the fallback threshold. There is no Corio indemnity anywhere in the Agreement, so nothing to narrow.

Upside items noted for the rationale only (not redlined): no coverage for Commerce One's breach of law, Commerce One-caused data breach, or gross negligence/wilful misconduct, and "its Customers" rather than affiliates. No redline proposed.
